      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, you're saying \"talossani\" means \"my wolf\"? I'm pretty sure the root there is \"talo\" (house) and the \"-ssa\" is the inessive case suffix. Also, \"kynsi\" usually means \"nail,\" not \"fur.\" Can you double check those definitions and the morphological breakdown? I need the actual structural analysis, not metaphors.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
